1
00:00:07,630 --> 00:00:09,390
Now, run!

2
00:00:09,390 --> 00:00:12,710
Show me you've got spirit!

3
00:00:13,300 --> 00:00:14,950
I think the same thing every time, but...

4
00:00:13,390 --> 00:00:16,470
Come on! Pick up the pace!

5
00:00:14,950 --> 00:00:17,910
This long-distance running 
after training sure is rough!

6
00:00:16,470 --> 00:00:19,560
This year's freshmen sure do have potential!

7
00:00:17,910 --> 00:00:20,340
You're embarrassing yourself, 
whining like that!

8
00:00:20,790 --> 00:00:23,380
F-Faster again?

9
00:00:24,060 --> 00:00:28,320
I'm about to keel over...

10
00:00:29,250 --> 00:00:31,550
Me too, to be honest!

11
00:00:31,550 --> 00:00:33,830
Looks like you've still got plenty of energy!

12
00:00:34,770 --> 00:00:37,960
Wh-Who has plenty of energy?

13
00:00:38,990 --> 00:00:42,690
That one girl over there...

14
00:00:42,690 --> 00:00:45,770
How much energy does she have?

15
00:00:46,980 --> 00:00:48,650
Well, that's Chris for you...

16
00:01:03,120 --> 00:01:06,080
<u>Reborn</u>

17
00:01:03,120 --> 00:01:06,080
to Master the Blade
     From Hero-King to Extraordinary Squire

18
00:01:03,120 --> 00:01:06,080
to Master the Blade
From Hero-King to Extraordinary Squire

19
00:02:19,150 --> 00:02:23,530
Episode 8    The Order to Protect Ripple

20
00:02:23,800 --> 00:02:25,950
Those are the upperclassmen.

21
00:02:25,950 --> 00:02:27,570
Seems like it.

22
00:02:27,570 --> 00:02:29,750
Everybody's here, right?

23
00:02:30,010 --> 00:02:34,190
I have very important news for you all!

24
00:02:34,190 --> 00:02:37,430
You'll get the official announcement 
at tomorrow's morning assembly,

25
00:02:37,430 --> 00:02:42,960
but we're going to have a guest: 
Ripple, the Hyral Menas.

26
00:02:46,020 --> 00:02:49,400
I see. I understand the situation.

27
00:02:50,240 --> 00:02:51,600
A Special-class Rune...

28
00:02:51,890 --> 00:02:54,110
That's Silva Eiren.

29
00:02:54,110 --> 00:02:58,190
The younger brother of Ledas Eiren, 
head of the Royal Guard,

30
00:02:58,190 --> 00:03:01,310
and the only Special-class 
Rune bearer at the academy.

31
00:03:01,620 --> 00:03:08,510
We are to protect Ripple and eliminate 
any magicite beasts that appear,

32
00:03:08,510 --> 00:03:12,450
while ensuring that nothing in the 
vicinity is damaged. Correct?

33
00:03:12,710 --> 00:03:14,830
Correct!

34
00:03:14,830 --> 00:03:17,470
We can't predict when Ripple's 
condition will strike,

35
00:03:17,470 --> 00:03:20,420
or when the magicite beasts will appear.

36
00:03:20,420 --> 00:03:23,140
Sorry for the trouble, everyone.

37
00:03:23,140 --> 00:03:26,620
So he's the strongest 
student at the academy.

38
00:03:26,620 --> 00:03:28,680
That's great. I'd love to fight him!

39
00:03:28,680 --> 00:03:31,090
That's all you ever think about.

40
00:03:31,090 --> 00:03:34,800
You've all been specially 
chosen from your grades.

41
00:03:34,800 --> 00:03:37,010
Each grade's members will form a team,

42
00:03:37,010 --> 00:03:40,810
and each team will take turns 
protecting Ripple for a day.

43
00:03:40,810 --> 00:03:44,420
Please isolate the magicite beasts 
from the surrounding area

44
00:03:44,420 --> 00:03:47,540
using a barrier generated by these Artifacts 
before attempting to eliminate them.

45
00:03:47,540 --> 00:03:53,120
We ask that you have someone who can create 
a barrier by Ripple's side at all times.

46
00:03:54,760 --> 00:03:56,540
I don't see a bow.

47
00:03:56,540 --> 00:03:58,160
I can't use any of these.

48
00:03:58,430 --> 00:04:00,650
I guess I'll take one.

49
00:04:00,650 --> 00:04:04,990
<i>If I transform my aether into mana, 
I might be able to generate a barrier.</i>

50
00:04:04,990 --> 00:04:07,140
There's no point in giving you that.

51
00:04:07,860 --> 00:04:11,270
A Runeless squire can't use 
one of those things.

52
00:04:11,270 --> 00:04:12,740
Keep your hands off them.

53
00:04:12,740 --> 00:04:14,590
Okay, got it!

54
00:04:15,190 --> 00:04:17,740
Wait! You don't need to—

55
00:04:17,740 --> 00:04:20,310
Rani, it's fine.

56
00:04:20,740 --> 00:04:24,320
What's a squire doing here, anyway?

57
00:04:24,320 --> 00:04:27,030
Having a Runeless here 
just puts the rest of us at risk.

58
00:04:27,030 --> 00:04:28,950
Leave, now.

59
00:04:28,950 --> 00:04:32,580
<i>Good grief. He's the highly strung, 
short-tempered type, right?</i>

60
00:04:32,580 --> 00:04:34,340
And not just the squire.

61
00:04:34,340 --> 00:04:37,140
We also have a traitor's 
blood relative in our midst.

62
00:04:37,140 --> 00:04:41,890
I can't entrust my life 
to the sister of the traitor Leon.

63
00:04:41,890 --> 00:04:44,430
Leone and Leon are different people.

64
00:04:44,430 --> 00:04:47,360
Even as an upperclassman, 
you can't talk to her like that!

65
00:04:47,360 --> 00:04:48,550
That's right!

66
00:04:48,550 --> 00:04:50,590
That's such a shallow thing to think!

67
00:04:50,590 --> 00:04:53,050
When you get to know her, you'll understand.

68
00:04:53,050 --> 00:04:54,290
What?

69
00:04:54,290 --> 00:04:56,640
No fighting, okay?

70
00:04:57,030 --> 00:04:59,980
Silva, I think that remark 
went a little far...

71
00:05:00,250 --> 00:05:01,900
In that case, Upperclassman Silva...

72
00:05:01,900 --> 00:05:06,660
How about determining our worthiness 
for the mission first-hand through battle?

73
00:05:06,660 --> 00:05:09,910
A battle? Between you people and me?

74
00:05:10,250 --> 00:05:11,230
Excuse me.

75
00:05:13,090 --> 00:05:15,910
I don't want to. I don't care enough.

76
00:05:16,420 --> 00:05:19,630
And if the squires are supposed to leave...

77
00:05:19,940 --> 00:05:24,120
then I'm a squire, so I'm leaving.

78
00:05:25,910 --> 00:05:28,170
Wait, Yua!

79
00:05:28,170 --> 00:05:29,690
What?

80
00:05:29,690 --> 00:05:31,650
I'm sleepy.

81
00:05:31,650 --> 00:05:34,060
Did you hear what I said?

82
00:05:34,060 --> 00:05:37,080
I need your help.

83
00:05:37,660 --> 00:05:38,660
Tee-hee.

84
00:05:39,880 --> 00:05:42,470
<i>It's hard to discern exactly 
what that "tee-hee" means.</i>

85
00:05:42,470 --> 00:05:45,400
You're the best student in the second year!

86
00:05:45,400 --> 00:05:47,480
We need you here!

87
00:05:47,480 --> 00:05:48,930
That's right, Yua!

88
00:05:48,930 --> 00:05:52,900
I don't know if we're strong 
enough to do this without you!

89
00:05:53,460 --> 00:05:54,940
Okay.

90
00:05:54,940 --> 00:05:55,900
I'll do it.

91
00:05:56,900 --> 00:06:00,070
Okay, Yua. Let's all fight Silva together—

92
00:06:00,070 --> 00:06:01,100
No.

93
00:06:02,480 --> 00:06:06,120
So you lack the courage to face me, then.

94
00:06:06,750 --> 00:06:09,300
I already know who's stronger.

95
00:06:09,900 --> 00:06:12,070
I don't like bullying the weak.

96
00:06:12,070 --> 00:06:13,320
What?

97
00:06:13,770 --> 00:06:17,350
Principal, did those two...

98
00:06:17,350 --> 00:06:20,720
Yes, they had a mock battle one time...

99
00:06:20,720 --> 00:06:23,330
Yua, you can't say that to his face!

100
00:06:20,720 --> 00:06:23,370
And Yua won?

101
00:06:23,330 --> 00:06:26,890
First he wants me to leave, 
then he wants a duel.

102
00:06:23,370 --> 00:06:27,250
Yes. Ever since then, 
they've been like oil and water.

103
00:06:26,890 --> 00:06:28,440
He's a pain in the butt.

104
00:06:27,940 --> 00:06:30,730
As the strongest of the freshmen,

105
00:06:28,440 --> 00:06:30,950
I'm not the one who proposed a battle.

106
00:06:30,730 --> 00:06:34,200
it'd be a huge help if you could get 
them to see eye to eye again...

107
00:06:35,130 --> 00:06:39,000
If you want me to beat the both 
of them at once, I'd be happy to!

108
00:06:40,510 --> 00:06:42,120
I'm sorry, everyone.

109
00:06:42,470 --> 00:06:45,100
This is my fault.

110
00:06:45,380 --> 00:06:48,600
I'm causing problems for you all...

111
00:06:49,390 --> 00:06:50,690
Ripple...

112
00:06:53,440 --> 00:06:54,590
Ripple?!

113
00:06:56,610 --> 00:06:58,380
Wh-What?

114
00:06:58,380 --> 00:06:59,900
Be careful, everyone!

115
00:06:59,900 --> 00:07:02,210
Theodore, get away from here!

116
00:07:02,210 --> 00:07:05,110
I'll put up a barrier! Be careful!

117
00:07:09,220 --> 00:07:10,060
Here they come!

118
00:07:10,750 --> 00:07:15,040
Ma'am, who's in charge today?

119
00:07:16,050 --> 00:07:19,570
May we third-year students 
have the first day?

120
00:07:19,570 --> 00:07:22,250
That's fine by me...

121
00:07:22,950 --> 00:07:24,430
Magicite beasts!

122
00:07:24,430 --> 00:07:25,930
They're demihuman!

123
00:07:29,090 --> 00:07:31,090
You all heard the principal.

124
00:07:31,090 --> 00:07:33,600
Nobody but us third-years 
can lay a hand on them—

125
00:07:37,430 --> 00:07:39,040
You there!

126
00:07:39,040 --> 00:07:40,640
I just said you can't lay a hand on them!

127
00:07:40,640 --> 00:07:41,470
I know!

128
00:07:41,470 --> 00:07:43,410
That's why I used my foot!

129
00:07:43,410 --> 00:07:46,970
That girl's a squire, but she's so strong!

130
00:07:48,630 --> 00:07:51,870
I can see why they called her here!

131
00:07:52,200 --> 00:07:53,200
And...

132
00:07:53,580 --> 00:07:56,400
She's so cute!

133
00:07:56,740 --> 00:07:58,900
We've got more important 
things to think about now!

134
00:07:58,900 --> 00:08:00,860
Everyone in my grade, fight!

135
00:08:02,380 --> 00:08:07,250
No amount of physical damage 
will hurt a magicite beast!

136
00:08:14,230 --> 00:08:17,670
<i>A gun Artifact? That's a rare sight.</i>

137
00:08:17,670 --> 00:08:19,380
<i>Let's see what he's capable—</i>

138
00:08:23,470 --> 00:08:24,710
Rani!

139
00:08:24,710 --> 00:08:26,700
Don't come running to me 
if he gets mad at you!

140
00:08:26,700 --> 00:08:30,040
But I didn't lay a hand on them!

141
00:08:30,040 --> 00:08:31,650
I shot them with my bow.

142
00:08:31,650 --> 00:08:33,280
Oh! That's fine, then!

143
00:08:33,280 --> 00:08:35,300
That's not what I meant!

144
00:08:35,300 --> 00:08:36,100
You can't selfishly—

145
00:08:35,810 --> 00:08:37,530
Who's being selfish?

146
00:08:38,530 --> 00:08:42,440
Ripple's going to suffer if someone 
here gets hurt, no matter who it is!

147
00:08:42,440 --> 00:08:46,080
Your pride isn't what matters here! 
We all need to work together!

148
00:08:46,080 --> 00:08:50,040
What? You don't have a Special-class Rune.

149
00:08:50,040 --> 00:08:51,140
You don't have the right—

150
00:08:50,430 --> 00:08:53,040
I've seen someone who does up close!

151
00:08:53,690 --> 00:08:58,160
You're going to be a holy knight and 
fight alongside a Hyral Menas, right?

152
00:08:58,520 --> 00:09:03,470
Then you should try to be more 
understanding of her than anyone here!

153
00:09:03,840 --> 00:09:05,790
<i>When she believes in something,</i>

154
00:09:05,790 --> 00:09:08,780
<i>she won't back down, 
no matter who she's talking to.</i>

155
00:09:08,780 --> 00:09:10,430
<i>That's the spirit!</i>

156
00:09:11,260 --> 00:09:12,990
Silva! More incoming!

157
00:09:13,820 --> 00:09:16,100
All right! Third-years, engage the enemy!

158
00:09:21,950 --> 00:09:26,070
I just happened to swing my spear, 
and it hit the enemy!

159
00:09:26,070 --> 00:09:29,170
And I guess my sword collided 
with something! Sorry!

160
00:09:30,030 --> 00:09:32,360
Why are you all like this?

161
00:09:32,360 --> 00:09:34,500
Now, now, Silva!

162
00:09:34,500 --> 00:09:39,590
Let's say it's the principal's orders! 
Everybody, engage the enemy!

163
00:09:39,590 --> 00:09:41,260
I'll do my best!

164
00:09:45,390 --> 00:09:46,760
Yua!

165
00:09:47,020 --> 00:09:48,510
You heard what she said, right?

166
00:09:48,510 --> 00:09:51,420
Don't be upset! Help fight!

167
00:09:51,860 --> 00:09:53,160
I'm sorry!

168
00:09:57,560 --> 00:09:58,580
Smack.

169
00:10:02,810 --> 00:10:04,000
Wow!

170
00:10:04,600 --> 00:10:07,960
<i>I may be under increased gravity right now,</i>

171
00:10:07,960 --> 00:10:10,420
<i>but this is the first time 
anyone's been faster than me.</i>

172
00:10:12,940 --> 00:10:13,850
Sorry.

173
00:10:13,850 --> 00:10:15,300
It's fine!

174
00:10:17,590 --> 00:10:19,130
Nice.

175
00:10:19,130 --> 00:10:22,980
Thank you! I'd love to battle you sometime!

176
00:10:22,980 --> 00:10:24,130
I'd rather not.

177
00:10:24,750 --> 00:10:27,110
I don't want to compare my 
strength with other people.

178
00:10:27,110 --> 00:10:28,990
Aww, come on!

179
00:10:28,990 --> 00:10:29,560
No.

180
00:10:29,560 --> 00:10:30,500
Please!

181
00:10:30,500 --> 00:10:31,340
Not a chance.

182
00:10:31,340 --> 00:10:32,720
I'm begging you!

183
00:10:31,880 --> 00:10:33,520
Wow, those two are incredible.

184
00:10:32,720 --> 00:10:33,480
Never.

185
00:10:33,480 --> 00:10:34,670
Please!

186
00:10:33,520 --> 00:10:34,970
This is so easy.

187
00:10:34,670 --> 00:10:35,530
No way.

188
00:10:34,970 --> 00:10:36,720
Stop gawking and fight!

189
00:10:42,070 --> 00:10:44,060
That should do it.

190
00:10:45,220 --> 00:10:46,490
Ripple!

191
00:10:47,520 --> 00:10:51,000
If it's the same as it was before, 
she should wake up soon.

192
00:10:54,970 --> 00:10:57,200
Good work, everyone.

193
00:10:57,200 --> 00:11:02,570
But this is only a way to keep the damage 
to a minimum, and not a solution.

194
00:11:02,570 --> 00:11:04,750
Do you have a solution?

195
00:11:04,750 --> 00:11:07,480
It's going to take time, 
but we'll do our best.

196
00:11:07,940 --> 00:11:10,960
I would appreciate it if you would!

197
00:11:12,760 --> 00:11:16,610
I don't know how much of this 
the school building can take.

198
00:11:16,610 --> 00:11:18,640
That's your fault!

199
00:11:18,640 --> 00:11:21,130
For not watching where you 
were hitting the enemy!

200
00:11:21,650 --> 00:11:24,100
We held back as best we could...

201
00:11:24,100 --> 00:11:25,590
Right? Um...

202
00:11:25,590 --> 00:11:27,570
My name's Inglis, Yua!

203
00:11:27,570 --> 00:11:31,540
In... Ingl... In...

204
00:11:32,480 --> 00:11:35,850
Yua's not good at learning people's names.

205
00:11:35,850 --> 00:11:37,750
That's right, Bean Sprout.

206
00:11:37,750 --> 00:11:40,410
See? She's known me for a year.

207
00:11:40,410 --> 00:11:42,620
The name's Morris, by the way. 
 Nice to meet you.

208
00:11:43,020 --> 00:11:45,770
Call me what you like, then, Yua!

209
00:11:47,320 --> 00:11:48,720
Okay, then...

210
00:11:49,830 --> 00:11:51,330
You can be Boobs.

211
00:11:52,920 --> 00:11:55,370
And if the upperclassmen had worked harder,

212
00:11:55,370 --> 00:11:57,640
we wouldn't have needed to do all that.

213
00:11:58,020 --> 00:12:02,870
I was just holding back so that my Artifact 
wouldn't destroy the building!

214
00:12:02,870 --> 00:12:04,610
Think when you fight!

215
00:12:04,940 --> 00:12:07,540
We were thinking, right, Boobs?

216
00:12:10,230 --> 00:12:12,690
<i>When I became king of an entire country,</i>

217
00:12:12,690 --> 00:12:15,550
<i>I never thought the day would 
come when I'd be called "Boobs."</i>

218
00:12:15,550 --> 00:12:17,970
<i>You never know what 
fate's got in store for you.</i>

219
00:12:22,880 --> 00:12:26,000
And that's what she decided 
to call you, Inglis?

220
00:12:26,000 --> 00:12:28,840
It's embarrassing.

221
00:12:28,840 --> 00:12:31,640
She didn't bother to learn my name either.

222
00:12:31,640 --> 00:12:33,420
What did she call you?

223
00:12:33,420 --> 00:12:35,180
"Lady Animal Ears."

224
00:12:35,890 --> 00:12:37,840
It doesn't bother me.

225
00:12:37,840 --> 00:12:40,240
What did she call you, Rafinha?

226
00:12:40,240 --> 00:12:41,720
"Little Devil."

227
00:12:41,720 --> 00:12:45,230
That thunder she brought down 
must've really scared her...

228
00:12:45,230 --> 00:12:47,360
I don't think it's fair.

229
00:12:49,170 --> 00:12:50,620
And Leone?

230
00:12:50,620 --> 00:12:52,040
"Boobs #2."

231
00:12:52,040 --> 00:12:53,890
"Two" for short.

232
00:12:55,400 --> 00:12:57,160
And you, Liselotte?

233
00:12:57,160 --> 00:12:59,450
C... "Curly Hair."

234
00:13:01,060 --> 00:13:03,180
Man, that sucks for all you guys!

235
00:13:03,180 --> 00:13:05,590
I'm more upset with Silva!

236
00:13:05,590 --> 00:13:07,370
What was his problem?

237
00:13:07,370 --> 00:13:09,390
He's so arrogant and nasty!

238
00:13:10,400 --> 00:13:14,840
He's a little wound up.

239
00:13:14,840 --> 00:13:18,320
But I think he'd be a good match for me.

240
00:13:18,720 --> 00:13:20,070
Checkmate.

241
00:13:20,740 --> 00:13:22,780
I-I lose.

242
00:13:22,780 --> 00:13:26,620
Chris is always good at whatever she does.

243
00:13:25,860 --> 00:13:27,160
Checkmate.

244
00:13:29,290 --> 00:13:31,210
I lose again...

245
00:13:31,690 --> 00:13:34,160
Would you like to play a game, Ripple?

246
00:13:34,420 --> 00:13:39,770
Nah, I'm not really into this stuff. 
I'm more of the physical type.

247
00:13:39,770 --> 00:13:41,790
How about a battle, then?

248
00:13:41,790 --> 00:13:45,120
A bit of exercise is good for the mind, too!

249
00:13:45,910 --> 00:13:51,670
Chris, we're here to <i>protect</i> Ripple!

250
00:13:51,670 --> 00:13:56,260
That's right. You're supposed 
to defend her, not fight her!

251
00:13:56,260 --> 00:13:57,200
Sure.

252
00:13:57,840 --> 00:13:59,550
Yeah, let's do it.

253
00:13:59,550 --> 00:14:01,320
R-Really?

254
00:14:01,630 --> 00:14:06,970
Miliera and Theodore were saying they 
wanted to see what happens when I fight.

255
00:14:07,490 --> 00:14:11,270
And I want to see your 
strength for myself, too.

256
00:14:11,780 --> 00:14:13,810
Wow, you sure look pleased!

257
00:14:17,150 --> 00:14:20,720
Well, I assumed you'd say that eventually.

258
00:14:21,390 --> 00:14:24,660
You know your students well, then.

259
00:14:25,210 --> 00:14:27,630
In that case, can we get started right away?

260
00:14:27,630 --> 00:14:30,120
Theodore, give it to her.

261
00:14:30,680 --> 00:14:32,600
Leone, here.

262
00:14:32,600 --> 00:14:35,790
It's the same shape as Leone's sword.

263
00:14:36,260 --> 00:14:37,320
What's this?

264
00:14:37,600 --> 00:14:39,960
A Greater Artifact.

265
00:14:39,960 --> 00:14:42,600
After the battle with the 
magicite beasts yesterday,

266
00:14:42,600 --> 00:14:47,270
it seemed safer to move them somewhere 
else than put up a barrier.

267
00:14:47,270 --> 00:14:49,510
So I asked Theodore for it.

268
00:14:50,160 --> 00:14:55,490
Its Gift moves everyone in its vicinity 
into a pocket space, isolating them.

269
00:14:56,460 --> 00:14:58,620
That's amazing!

270
00:14:58,620 --> 00:15:03,470
Leone's Rune is the most compatible 
with it in terms of element.

271
00:15:03,470 --> 00:15:05,550
Mine?

272
00:15:06,340 --> 00:15:10,500
We'd like you to test how strong 
the space is and how long it holds.

273
00:15:10,500 --> 00:15:14,600
So please conduct your battle 
within the effect of this Artifact.

274
00:15:14,600 --> 00:15:17,880
If it works, we can share it 
with the other teams.

275
00:15:18,800 --> 00:15:22,360
Okay, Leone. Do it right now! Now! Now!

276
00:15:23,930 --> 00:15:27,740
She can't wait to fight, can she?

277
00:15:27,740 --> 00:15:29,010
Go ahead.

278
00:15:29,010 --> 00:15:32,060
We'd like to see how it 
works from inside, too.

279
00:15:32,530 --> 00:15:35,020
Okay, then. Let's see...

280
00:15:37,310 --> 00:15:38,960
Focus your mind.

281
00:15:42,170 --> 00:15:44,390
Leone, you can do it!

282
00:15:44,760 --> 00:15:46,850
You don't need to force it.

283
00:15:46,850 --> 00:15:49,970
Just give yourself over to 
the flow the Rune creates...

284
00:15:49,970 --> 00:15:51,280
Okay...

285
00:15:56,900 --> 00:15:59,010
Yes, just like that...

286
00:16:02,520 --> 00:16:03,680
I did it!

287
00:16:03,680 --> 00:16:06,050
It's like the Labyrinth of Trials...

288
00:16:07,660 --> 00:16:10,700
You okay, Leone? You feeling all right?

289
00:16:11,160 --> 00:16:13,120
I-I'm okay.

290
00:16:13,690 --> 00:16:15,330
You can start.

291
00:16:16,020 --> 00:16:17,230
Thanks!

292
00:16:17,780 --> 00:16:19,470
Let's do this, Ripple!

293
00:16:19,470 --> 00:16:20,280
Yeah!

294
00:16:22,980 --> 00:16:26,030
<i>It's been so long since 
I last fought a Hyral Menas.</i>

295
00:16:26,030 --> 00:16:27,910
<i>I can barely contain my excitement!</i>

296
00:16:28,220 --> 00:16:31,130
Miliera, block any stray shots, okay?

297
00:16:31,130 --> 00:16:32,830
Okay!

298
00:16:32,830 --> 00:16:37,910
Start light and gradually ramp it up, okay?

299
00:16:38,700 --> 00:16:39,780
Roger.

300
00:16:39,780 --> 00:16:41,100
Come on, then.

301
00:16:41,740 --> 00:16:42,910
Here I go!

302
00:16:47,640 --> 00:16:48,980
<i>A head-on fight!</i>

303
00:16:50,530 --> 00:16:52,210
Nice punch!

304
00:16:55,830 --> 00:16:58,130
M-My goodness.

305
00:16:58,130 --> 00:17:01,950
Inglis is attacking with incredible speed.

306
00:17:01,950 --> 00:17:06,570
But Ripple's dodging it all easily!

307
00:17:09,730 --> 00:17:11,470
That was a little close!

308
00:17:11,900 --> 00:17:15,260
I'll do this my usual way, then.

309
00:17:16,870 --> 00:17:20,380
Close-up fighting isn't my style.

310
00:17:20,380 --> 00:17:21,610
A gun?

311
00:17:21,990 --> 00:17:25,750
Now I understand why you said 
Silva would be a good match for you.

312
00:17:25,750 --> 00:17:27,010
Yup.

313
00:17:27,700 --> 00:17:28,750
Here I go.

314
00:17:35,240 --> 00:17:36,600
An ice blade!

315
00:17:38,410 --> 00:17:42,570
<i>I made an ice blade with magic! It worked!</i>

316
00:17:42,840 --> 00:17:46,950
<i>If I'd waited until the last second to dodge, 
I wouldn't have given her that opening.</i>

317
00:17:46,600 --> 00:17:48,840
Nice. Here I go!

318
00:17:46,950 --> 00:17:48,200
<i>I'll address that next time.</i>

319
00:17:52,040 --> 00:17:53,240
Oh, no!

320
00:17:54,460 --> 00:17:57,370
I can handle this much.

321
00:17:59,760 --> 00:18:04,500
Nothing stronger, though!

322
00:18:04,500 --> 00:18:06,880
That means I can give it my all!

323
00:18:06,880 --> 00:18:09,650
Please listen to what I'm saying!

324
00:18:11,340 --> 00:18:14,740
<i>I need to get close and take the offensive!</i>

325
00:18:15,820 --> 00:18:20,230
<i>Ripple's strength is her ability 
to keep her distance at all times.</i>

326
00:18:21,050 --> 00:18:24,250
<i>I need to overcome that and win!</i>

327
00:18:24,560 --> 00:18:27,230
They're getting closer!

328
00:18:27,230 --> 00:18:32,220
Inglis is trying to get 
close enough to attack!

329
00:18:33,280 --> 00:18:35,460
I'm not going to stop moving.

330
00:18:35,460 --> 00:18:37,040
I'll catch up to you!

331
00:18:40,460 --> 00:18:42,180
You look so happy!

332
00:18:42,560 --> 00:18:45,390
<i>If I can get one step closer, 
she'll be in range!</i>

333
00:18:47,060 --> 00:18:48,340
Another gun?

334
00:18:48,680 --> 00:18:50,820
Yup. Dual handguns.

335
00:18:57,190 --> 00:18:58,330
There!

336
00:18:58,330 --> 00:18:59,140
I'm not done yet!

337
00:18:59,450 --> 00:19:00,960
Now it's my turn to go on the offensive.

338
00:19:00,960 --> 00:19:02,420
Can you get close to me?

339
00:19:02,420 --> 00:19:04,560
I can't see an opening from either of them!

340
00:19:04,560 --> 00:19:05,610
Chris!

341
00:19:06,210 --> 00:19:07,460
<i>What do I do?</i>

342
00:19:07,460 --> 00:19:10,390
<i>Wait for her to run out of ammo?</i>

343
00:19:10,820 --> 00:19:14,220
<i>Or will my stamina run out first?</i>

344
00:19:16,470 --> 00:19:18,800
<i>She's not moving?</i>

345
00:19:19,270 --> 00:19:20,420
<i>So that's it.</i>

346
00:19:20,420 --> 00:19:24,620
<i>I'm fighting at her range, 
which means I'm moving and she's not.</i>

347
00:19:24,620 --> 00:19:25,690
<i>So maybe...</i>

348
00:19:27,330 --> 00:19:30,850
<i>If I turn toward her and become 
a smaller target...</i>

349
00:19:31,120 --> 00:19:33,330
<i>The bullets will have to be closer together!</i>

350
00:19:36,610 --> 00:19:37,330
<i>Got you!</i>

351
00:19:40,130 --> 00:19:41,150
Take this!

352
00:19:45,260 --> 00:19:46,230
There's my opening!

353
00:19:51,450 --> 00:19:52,670
She'll hit them!

354
00:19:56,670 --> 00:19:58,120
Are you okay?

355
00:19:58,870 --> 00:20:00,590
Oww...

356
00:20:00,590 --> 00:20:02,990
You not only deflected my bullets, 
you threw them back at me?

357
00:20:02,990 --> 00:20:04,700
Are you some kind of pervert?

358
00:20:04,700 --> 00:20:08,480
Miliera, thanks for catching me 
with your barrier.

359
00:20:08,480 --> 00:20:11,910
No, I didn't do anything.

360
00:20:12,430 --> 00:20:17,170
I thought you were going to slam into it, 
but when you touched the barrier,

361
00:20:17,170 --> 00:20:20,240
it disappeared like it had been sucked away.

362
00:20:20,960 --> 00:20:23,910
You mean your mana was drained away?

363
00:20:24,780 --> 00:20:26,470
Um, can we continue?

364
00:20:25,370 --> 00:20:29,430
Can we test that with 
someone else's Artifact?

365
00:20:30,460 --> 00:20:31,950
You can use mine.

366
00:20:31,950 --> 00:20:34,030
Um, our fight...

367
00:20:34,030 --> 00:20:34,870
Chris!

368
00:20:34,870 --> 00:20:36,670
They're having a serious conversation!

369
00:20:36,670 --> 00:20:39,630
Touch this, Ripple.

370
00:20:45,210 --> 00:20:46,660
Does anything feel strange?

371
00:20:47,190 --> 00:20:49,090
Nothing.

372
00:20:50,130 --> 00:20:54,470
Miliera, now you borrow her Artifact.

373
00:20:54,470 --> 00:20:56,610
The angel wings?

374
00:20:56,610 --> 00:20:58,770
I'm a little old for those...

375
00:21:05,130 --> 00:21:06,990
Go ahead, Ripple.

376
00:21:18,610 --> 00:21:20,540
It's absorbing her mana, 
just like we thought.

377
00:21:21,510 --> 00:21:23,860
But only Miliera's!

378
00:21:24,360 --> 00:21:27,190
Maybe it's because Hyral Menases 
can only take power

379
00:21:27,190 --> 00:21:30,600
from a holy knight with a Special-class Rune?

380
00:21:30,970 --> 00:21:34,930
Yes. The weapon transformation power, 
which normally requires intent on her part

381
00:21:34,930 --> 00:21:39,760
and the power of a Special Rune, has been 
twisted into absorbing mana on its own.

382
00:21:40,180 --> 00:21:43,250
And when a certain amount 
has been absorbed...

383
00:21:46,080 --> 00:21:48,110
It summons magicite beasts.

384
00:21:48,490 --> 00:21:50,980
Sorry, Inglis.

385
00:21:51,430 --> 00:21:54,350
Take care of them for me...

386
00:21:54,790 --> 00:21:56,430
Ripple!

387
00:21:56,430 --> 00:21:58,130
I-I'm sorry!

388
00:21:59,620 --> 00:22:01,550
I can't keep this up anymore!

389
00:23:46,070 --> 00:23:51,070
m 0 0 l 100 0 100 100 0 100

390
00:23:46,070 --> 00:23:51,070
Your
nickname
 can be...

391
00:23:46,070 --> 00:23:51,070
m 0 0 l 100 0 100 100 0 100

392
00:23:46,070 --> 00:23:51,070
"Principal
Who's
Trying
To
Look
Young"

393
00:23:46,070 --> 00:23:51,070
Comic by Kuromura Moto

